.\" sliver-stylesheet(5). Spec: docs/styling.md and ADR-0004 (ash).
.TH SLIVER\-STYLESHEET 5 2026-10-12 "sliver 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sliver\-stylesheet \- Touch Bar stylesheet (style.css)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliver/style.css
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Touch Bar is styled with a CSS stylesheet, like waybar's
.BR style.css .
The file sits next to the configuration
.RB ( sliver\-config (5)),
or wherever its
.B stylesheet
key points.
It is loaded on top of the built\-in theme chosen by the configuration's
.B theme
key (default
.BR sliver ).
.B style\-dark.css
and
.B style\-light.css
are used instead when present, following the desktop's color scheme.
.PP
Nothing in a stylesheet can blank the bar.
Each problem is reported as
.IB file : line : col : " message"\fR,
and only the offending declaration, selector or rule is dropped.
The built\-in safe layer of
.BR sliverd (8)
never uses your stylesheet.
.SH TREE
.EX
bar      classes: layer\-<name>, layout\-<name>, <bar name>, locked, dimmed
+\- zone   class .zone\-<name>, plus the zone's configured class
   +\- module  #<type>, .module, .<instance>, state classes, script and config classes
      +\- trough       sliders only
         +\- highlight   the filled part
         +\- slider      the knob
.EE
.PP
Module ids are the type with
.B /
replaced by
.BR \- :
.BR #clock ,
.BR #battery ,
.BR #custom\-vpn ,
.BR #key\-f1 ,
.BR #group\-control\-strip .
An instance becomes a class
.RB ( battery#bat2
is
.BR #battery.bat2 ).
State classes include
.BR .warning ,
.BR .critical ,
.BR .charging ,
.BR .muted ,
.BR .playing ,
.B .on
(toggles that are on),
.B .error
(a failed script) and
.BR .drawer\-child .
Items published by apps also get
.BR .dbus ,
.B .app
or
.BR .status ,
their type
.RB ( .button ,
.BR .slider ,
\&...), their own classes, and
.B .focused\-app
while their app is focused.
.SH SELECTORS
.BR * ,
.BR bar ,
.BR zone ,
.BR module ,
.BI # id\fR,
.BI . class\fR,
.B :active
(pressed),
.B :checked
(a toggle that is on),
.BR :disabled ,
.BR :first\-child ,
.BR :last\-child ,
.BR :not( \fIsimple\fP ) ,
descendant
.RB ( "a b" )
and child
.RB ( "a > b" )
combinators, and comma lists.
.B :hover
and
.B :focus
are accepted but never match on a touch strip.
Sibling combinators aren't supported.
Precedence is standard CSS:
.BR !important ,
then specificity, then later rules.
.SH PROPERTIES
.TP
.B color
Labels and symbolic icons (inherited).
.TP
.BR background ", " background\-color
Plain colors only.
.TP
.BR border ", " border\-width ", " border\-color ", " border\-style ", " border\-radius
.TP
.BR padding ", " margin
1\(en4 lengths, or the per\-side forms
.RB ( padding\-left ,
\&...).
.TP
.BR font\-family ", " font\-size ", " font\-weight
Inherited.
Labels shrink (down to half size) to fit, then are ellipsized.
.TP
.BR \-sliver\-icon\-size " (" \-gtk\-icon\-size )
Inherited.
.TP
.B opacity
0\(en1 or a percentage.
It multiplies down the tree.
.TP
.BR min\-width ", " min\-height
On modules, the floor for auto widths.
On
.B trough
and
.BR slider ,
the track's length and thickness and the knob's size.
.TP
.B gap
Between zones (on
.BR bar ),
between modules (on
.BR zone ),
and between icon and label (on
.BR module ).
.TP
.B transition
Accepted, but not animated yet.
.PP
Lengths are
.BR px ,
.BR pt ,
.B em
or bare numbers (pixels).
.BR inherit ,
.B initial
and
.B unset
work everywhere.
Colors are anything CSS accepts, plus GTK's
.BI @ name\fR,
.BR alpha() ,
.BR shade() ,
.BR mix() ,
.B lighter()
and
.BR darker() .
.SH AT\-RULES
.TP
.BI "@define\-color " "name value" ;
Must come before use.
.TP
.BI "@import """ path """;"
Relative to the importing file.
.B @import """sliver:classic"";"
imports a built\-in theme.
Imports nest up to 8 levels deep.
.PP
Other at\-rules are reported and skipped.
.SH THEMES
.TP
.B sliver
The default: the macOS Touch Bar look.
Toggles that are on and slider fills use
.BR @accent ,
which the agent takes from the desktop's accent color.
.TP
.B light
Dark text on light keys, also with
.BR @accent .
The Touch Bar is an OLED panel, so lit pixels cost power: this theme draws more than the dark ones.
.TP
.B high\-contrast
White outlines and larger bold text on black.
A pressed key inverts, and a toggle that is on is solid yellow, so no state depends on hue alone.
.TP
.B classic
tiny\-dfr's look.
.PP
Every theme gets the desktop's
.BR @accent .
An unknown name is reported and
.B sliver
is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
@import "sliver:classic";
@define\-color accent #3584e4;

module            { border\-radius: 10px; padding: 0 18px; }
module:active     { background: @accent; }
#battery.critical { background: #c01c28; }
#custom\-vpn.connected { color: #33d17a; }
\&.zone\-main        { background: alpha(white, 0.06); }
bar.layer\-fn module { background: #1e1e24; }
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR waybar\-styles (5)
.PP
.I docs/styling.md
in the sliver sources.
